September 10, 1994

Welcome to Fax-IT Version 3.0, modified for Cnet!

NEW FEATURES:

o Phonebook support.  Thanks Glenn!!
o External config. files to make setting up _alot_ easier.
o Fixes of some bugs that popped up as a result of my V1.0 conversion
o Clearer (hopefully) CNet setup instructions

Many Thanks to DAVID WEEKS for pointing out that nifty GetUser value that points to
Cnet's _edbuff files.  As of this version, you'll no longer need to enter in
a DataPath.

INSTALLATION:

This is the great part:  

o Create a FAX-IT directory in your Doors: path. 
o (You will need a Doors: assign, if you don't already have one) 
o Put the contents of the FAX-IT directory in the archive into your FAX-IT directory. 
o Adopt FaxIT as an Arexx program, 
o Adjust the configuration files as in Glenn's instructions.
o YOU'RE DONE!

** NOTE **
            If you are upgrading from V1.0 you will need to replace
            all the files in the FAX-IT directory with the new ones and
            redo all your changes you made.
                                                    Sorry!

If you're a USRobotics user and run Trapdoor on the same line as GPFax, you might
want to have a look in the "USRobotics_Users/" directory.  I put the AutoCall.GPF 
that I'm using on my system there along with some words of.. 
::ahem!:: ..encouragement <g>.

See Glenn's FAX-IT.doc for other IMPORTANT information you'll need to get up and 
runnning properly.

Also please note that Glenn's program is Shareware. Please respect his distribution
wishes.

DISCLAIMER:

This CNet modification of Fax-IT is guaranteed to take up space on your hardrive
no other guarantees are made or implied.  It works great on my system, yours might
blow up.  Life is funny that way.

